I enter the small clinic.
Today there are many people in the clinic.
I go near the counter.
There is a woman there.
"Madam, my name is Maya," I say.
"I am not well today."
"My appointment is at ten today."
She looks and says, "Maya, you may sit there."
I go to the waiting room.
I sit on a chair there.
There are many sick people in the room.
There is an elderly man near me.
He is coughing again and again.
A young mother is also there.
Her baby is restless.
The baby is crying loudly.
The mother comforts him.
There is an ache in my entire body too.
I wait patiently for my name to be called.
